cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Divisible-Sandpile-Percolation"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Quantitative
  explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile" (Bou-Rabee and
  Panagiotis, arXiv:2609.02829): for every d >= 2 the toppled set of the
  divisible sandpile percolates for every mean close enough to one
  (Theorem 1.1), the level sets {u_t > c h(t)} of the finite-time odometer at
  mean one percolate at an explicit dimension-dependent scale h(t)
  (Theorem 1.2), and the quantitative explosion and scaling results at mean
  one in every dimension (Theorem 1.3), together with every lemma,
  proposition and corollary of the paper.  Sixteen results the paper cites
  without proof are taken as explicit hypotheses of the theorems that use
  them.  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom, and each of
  the twelve main theorems has a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - divisible sandpile
  - percolation
  - optimal stopping
  - membrane model
license: Apache-2.0
